--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
Lazy-wave power cable through a bend stiffener at a clamped hang-off on a vessel in a JONSWAP sea
-- The cable, vessel motion and sea of lazy_wave_vessel_rao.dat, with a 4 m polyurethane bend
-- stiffener at the hang-off: a 0.4 m cylindrical root of 0.45 m outer diameter and a 3.6 m cone
-- to 0.18 m, bored to 0.17 m (E = 50 MPa, 1150 kg/m^3). At the root the sleeve is about five
-- times as stiff in bending as the cable (EI 9.9e4 against 1.99e4 N m^2). The root is clamped
-- (Rigid) along the static hang-off tangent; BendMom1N1 is the root moment, the curvature
-- channels sample the stiffener (nodes 14 and 27, 2 m and 4 m from the root) and the bare cable
-- just past its tip (node 34). The 0.152 m elements give 27 elements over the stiffener.
